        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:22:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126324,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are most common on fingernails. They originate at the distal nail matrix and involve the nail bed and hyponychium {26518173; 29729116}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:22:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126325,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Onychopapilloma usually occurs in adults, with only rare paediatric cases reported. These lesions typically present with longitudinal erythronychia, a reddish nail streak and/or yellowish discolouration, sometimes beginning in a wedge-shaped contour in the distal matrix. Splinter haemorrhage is also common, as is distal subungual hyperkeratosis, often forming a spicule. These are as large as 5&ndash;6&nbsp;mm in width and are often more centrally placed. Distal nail plate splitting, fissuring or notching, and onycholysis can occur. Punctate haemorrhage has also been described. Onychopapilloma can show different patterns, including pigmented (often due to melanocytic activation) and those presenting with leukonychia {26518173; 29729116; 34396563}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:22:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126326,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Onychopapilloma is a relatively common and probably underreported benign epithelial proliferation of the nail unit; its incidence has not been formally studied {26518173; 29729116}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T08:22:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
